  "term": "Brief Psychiatric Rating Scale",
  "definition": "The Brief Psychiatric Rating Scale is a rating scale with 18 symptom areas meant to reflect relatively separate aspects of observable psychopathology. It was first developed to make treatment-response assessment more efficient in psychopharmacology research and was later adapted for other uses.",
